# One prompt → one card (no second build)

**Meaning (user intent):**  
If a design prompt was already used once to build a gallery card + animation (example: `src/templates/landing-page/3d-portfolio/prompt.js` → **3D Portfolio**), that **same prompt must never be used again** to build another card (e.g. “3D Portfolio 2.0”).

## Before any new template

1. Collect every existing file: `src/templates/**/prompt.js`.
2. Also read `meta.fullPrompt` from `src/templates/index.js` registry.
3. Compare the **new prompt body** the user pasted to those files (trim whitespace only).
4. If it matches (or is the same design body with only a new title/version name):

**STOP. Do not create folders, routes, components, or cards.**

Say clearly:

> **Blocked — this prompt was already used.**  
> Card: **`<title>`** · `prompt.js`: `src/templates/<category>/<id>/prompt.js`  
> Same prompt diye 2nd time animation/card banano jabe na. Existing template reuse koro, ba notun/different prompt dao.

## Allowed

- Edit/fix the **existing** template that owns that `prompt.js`
- A **different** prompt → new card under the right tab folder

## Not allowed

- Same `prompt.js` content under a new name/folder
- “2.0 / remake / copy” with the identical prompt text
